              "text": "వంకర (vaṅkara) matches Sanskrit vaṅkara (CDIAL 11193), a lexicon word for \"bend of a river\"; CDIAL only infers the sense \"crooked\". CDIAL ties vaṅka, \"bent, crooked\", to a probably non-Aryan word-group."
